cts an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Enovix Corporation is a small-cap industrials business with a $351M market cap on $32M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +72% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -230% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and -142% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $114M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -8.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 16.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 155% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 566% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry wi